No, you aren't going crazy – Apple has quietly made a backend change to the App Store app in iOS that switches the location of the Updates tab and renames it to make it more prominent.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2022/01/iOS-App-Store-General-Feature-Dock.jpg" alt="" width="2250" height="1266" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-833992" /><br/>
In the App Store app, you can see the change by tapping your profile picture in the top-right corner. The "Apps & Purchase History" tab used to be at the top the list, but it has switched places with "Updates," which is now called "App Updates."<br/>
<br/>
The change was made by Apple without issuing a software update and is evident on both iOS 26.4.1 and the iOS 26.5 beta. <br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/04/app-updates-app-store-ios.jpeg" alt="app store" width="1920" height="1080" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1045205" /><br/>
